{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","id":"pg_2fe6be43485f5cd494103bd0b2076fac","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/betterforall-self-improving-agents-prior-work-md-5f7823732d87-3bd0b2076fac.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_dc4992f6b06e5b7689ab09c593acc135"],"title":"BetterForAll/self-improving-agents/PRIOR_WORK.md @ 5f7823732d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","id":"pg_3c526060944b573e8f4d5626e239e65f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/betterforall-self-improving-agents-requirements-txt-5f7823732d87-5626e239e65f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ee189b1a23b7581d8ad38a3f39547018"],"title":"BetterForAll/self-improving-agents/requirements.txt @ 5f7823732d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0825d9b0e8687c769216166fdb299714053fdfa155db7ea5471ed8e3bd11ae10"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Level 3 (hyperagent/) has a meta-agent that rewrites the source of task_agent.py and meta_agent.py, with an immutable seed/ reference, live agent_code/ copies, and versioned generations/ snapshots."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0bc4802f7de30dd2f1cdd9662f3ed9ad003e6045e5b7e2ae88212abf3bb15ed4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Level 2 (feedback-loop/) adds a reviewer agent that returns structured feedback (issue type, severity, fix suggestion, confidence, detected pattern) explaining why a solution failed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_19a0eee0ba107a0ddb18d99ad3f27112b746e4c3976f1ca7935d4aba9006bc96"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each level is run via a run.py entry point (e.g. python autoresearch/run.py) with a --task flag selecting tasks such as snake, support, or email_validation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1df0d851293d033a7673e0ce3e0f918a93633f344ead8594917281c1655e7ac7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"run_all.py runs experiments across all levels and generates comparison analysis, supporting --levels/--tasks filters and a --fresh flag to ignore previous results; analyze_results.py performs cross-level comparison after experiments are done."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3635219370eec55e0ecfdf9529f5a9c497b299772a7a475768c7e546ca20e66d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"HyperAgent rewrites are validated by a three-stage crash recovery: compile check, import check, and signature check; invalid rewrites revert to the last valid generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_37d669749a1aa9d659d22f1371bb6089d098315e785f42762f5910572a1b24f8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup requires installing requirements.txt via pip and creating a .env file in the repo root containing a GEMINI_API_KEY obtained from Google AI Studio."},{"claim_ids":["clm_435cbe12a8f0f615010d13bb0e01d8342346e3d50f66b48033a15e25253f3544"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"HyperAgent is a simplification of Meta's HyperAgents (DGM-H): it uses folder-based versioning instead of Docker containers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_450b80a4589363c19dd28eee16b4c76a2f440bdb97fc4839cbc23a350792ed18"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Level 4a (Arena Single) pits one code agent against one test agent in adversarial co-evolution without tournament or population dynamics; 4b adds tournament selection where the worst agents are replaced by mutated winners."},{"claim_ids":["clm_51e11ff704badfb13491898d069d20db68b7748c442be796ec5e95428f9bb1f5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Level 2 uses asymmetric information: the worker gets a small prompt with just the code, while the reviewer sees full history and prior feedback to spot cross-iteration patterns."},{"claim_ids":["clm_546ec871b016f409478943efd740748638af2072056e095487e4d61ed4559723"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Level 1 (autoresearch/) is a single-agent loop: the LLM proposes code, it is written to a file, benchmarked, kept if better, and repeated; bad proposals revert immediately."},{"claim_ids":["clm_709413796f564831061a919454bea05436e47a82627baf60c852b71846519bfe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework is task-agnostic: a new task is a folder in tasks/ with config.py (task name, metric, direction, prompt builder), initial_solution.py, and a benchmark.py that prints 'metric_name:value' to stdout."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b2959b1a14e2b33efbbaeed7e88caecdb96af78e57a504f170a30b79db7e4b87"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All levels share tasks/checkpoint.py for resumable checkpointing using sequence-numbered JSON files with atomic writes (write to .tmp then os.replace), keeping only the last three checkpoints."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bcc5ed44ba5fa941733988366c022b83dfc64d30bc8d963ce970b2f3ba2e11f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In Arena Loop, code agents are described as mini-HyperAgents that can mutate their own propose() function, so the code-generating code itself evolves."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d6243040169d98da0b1a5c247c38910c14cfafcc6aae1dd1964d5d642b725f36"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project defines four levels of self-improving code agents, each adding one key idea, from a simple improvement loop to an adversarial arena with self-modifying agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df7163e766e5e41ca37312726e33c4ac886d4ea4c7f407019df11cf2007853c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project frames itself as independent research comparing existing self-improving code-agent approaches and proposing new ones, with lineage traced to AlphaGo/RLVR, AutoResearch, HyperAgents, and GAN-style co-evolution."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0825d9b0e8687c769216166fdb299714053fdfa155db7ea5471ed8e3bd11ae10","clm_0bc4802f7de30dd2f1cdd9662f3ed9ad003e6045e5b7e2ae88212abf3bb15ed4","clm_19a0eee0ba107a0ddb18d99ad3f27112b746e4c3976f1ca7935d4aba9006bc96","clm_1df0d851293d033a7673e0ce3e0f918a93633f344ead8594917281c1655e7ac7","clm_3635219370eec55e0ecfdf9529f5a9c497b299772a7a475768c7e546ca20e66d","clm_37d669749a1aa9d659d22f1371bb6089d098315e785f42762f5910572a1b24f8","clm_435cbe12a8f0f615010d13bb0e01d8342346e3d50f66b48033a15e25253f3544","clm_450b80a4589363c19dd28eee16b4c76a2f440bdb97fc4839cbc23a350792ed18","clm_51e11ff704badfb13491898d069d20db68b7748c442be796ec5e95428f9bb1f5","clm_546ec871b016f409478943efd740748638af2072056e095487e4d61ed4559723","clm_709413796f564831061a919454bea05436e47a82627baf60c852b71846519bfe","clm_b2959b1a14e2b33efbbaeed7e88caecdb96af78e57a504f170a30b79db7e4b87","clm_bcc5ed44ba5fa941733988366c022b83dfc64d30bc8d963ce970b2f3ba2e11f4","clm_d6243040169d98da0b1a5c247c38910c14cfafcc6aae1dd1964d5d642b725f36","clm_df7163e766e5e41ca37312726e33c4ac886d4ea4c7f407019df11cf2007853c7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","id":"pg_4a8b82f733e15ec58087e76cdb7f8205","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/betterforall-self-improving-agents-readme-md-5f7823732d87-e76cdb7f8205.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f718246686d85a4fa768db72f9e241cd"],"title":"BetterForAll/self-improving-agents/README.md @ 5f7823732d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","id":"pg_8ae1d141c4a5592db864c4c277241ba3","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/betterforall-self-improving-agents-claude-md-5f7823732d87-c4c277241ba3.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_90406d2919885b14b8d5e26dc21e112c"],"title":"BetterForAll/self-improving-agents/CLAUDE.md @ 5f7823732d87","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3463f9d610c8dc6a766bad608c5e5a04d9fb7385a2b98eb27059e7a33a4d5930"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cross-validation shows Levels 1-3 scored 90-100% on email_validation's original 20 tests but dropped to 62-66% on the expanded 50-case adversarial suite, while Arena levels held at 70% on the combined suite."},{"claim_ids":["clm_70559fc3ab565d228764941c42db1cffbaba2f0a46ec4681726845199516f74a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Experiments used Gemini 2.5 Flash across five levels and three tasks (email_validation, snake, support) in 15 total experiments, with per-level metrics, costs, and token counts reported."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9330320c5a646097cdfdf3a2af2509ded50ce4fea9819d67d6d57cf4b7fb9cdf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"For support, rubric-based boolean scoring (keyword match plus LLM YES/NO fallback) reduced judge noise from over 30 points to under 7; Feedback Loop scored highest (82.091) on the expanded 19 questions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ef49a4f6948d2520039c9289c30bd8c1cf483950fa1fce48b69798b9031e3fd3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The results document acknowledges single runs per experiment (N=1, no error bars), a small task set of three tasks, and a single model (Gemini 2.5 Flash), so findings may not generalize."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3463f9d610c8dc6a766bad608c5e5a04d9fb7385a2b98eb27059e7a33a4d5930","clm_70559fc3ab565d228764941c42db1cffbaba2f0a46ec4681726845199516f74a","clm_9330320c5a646097cdfdf3a2af2509ded50ce4fea9819d67d6d57cf4b7fb9cdf","clm_ef49a4f6948d2520039c9289c30bd8c1cf483950fa1fce48b69798b9031e3fd3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_146197f74bbb419c80f9b21a19f79497","id":"pg_999747499fc352a4b2998362c908e9b4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/betterforall-self-improving-agents-experiment-results-md-5f7823732d87-8362c908e9b4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_